WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.402
-Our first guest tonight is
a very talented actress you know

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:06.639
from films like "50 First
Dates," "Charlie's Angels,"

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:07.773
and "Never Been Kissed."

00:00:07.773 --> 00:00:10.210
She now hosts
"The Drew Barrymore Show."

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:13.379
Please welcome back to the show
Drew Barrymore, everybody!

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:15.314
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:25.224 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:25.224 --> 00:00:35.101 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:39.172
Yay, Drew Barrymore, everybody!
Please!

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:41.740
-Hi, guys. How are you?

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:42.809
Thanks for having me.

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:44.677
-Drew, I'm so happy you're here.

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:48.113
-Me, too, because
I almost wasn't.

00:00:48.113 --> 00:00:50.083
-Well, you were supposed to be
here a few weeks ago.

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:51.084
-Yes, I was.

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:53.519
-And it was a day-of
cancelation.

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:55.388
This is very rare.
-What happened?

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:57.056
Did someone else
fall off the wagon?

00:00:57.056 --> 00:00:59.325
-No, when you canceled on us,
day-of.

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:03.362
-Not in 20 years have I canceled
on anyone, ever.

00:01:03.362 --> 00:01:05.698
-Yes.
-I am very consistent.

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:08.067
-And yet here you were
very sick.

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:09.435
Not COVID,
but you were very sick.

00:01:09.435 --> 00:01:11.104
-I had full-Blown bronchitis,

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:13.139
which I did not know
at the time.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:15.341
And I've known you for so long

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:17.510
that I didn't want
a rep to call.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:20.512
I feel like we're too knowing of
each other for that.

00:01:20.512 --> 00:01:22.949
And I didn't want it to be like,
you know, surface.

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:26.686
So I decided to let you know
on my own terms

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:28.922
so that you felt it was true.

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:31.591
-So I didn't think you were
dodging or something came up.

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:33.759
You recorded an audio message
of yourself

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:35.861
to prove how sick you were.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.861 --> 00:01:38.264
And it was like 45 seconds,
Drew,

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:40.500
and I could not make it
more than three.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.502
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:45.671
-Oh, my God. And I have to
admit, I was so sick that I

00:01:45.671 --> 00:01:47.807
feel, like, a little bit
blackout-y about it.

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:51.610
Like, I was like, "I want to let
Seth know, with all my heart,

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:53.679
that something's really wrong."

00:01:53.679 --> 00:01:56.349
-The thing is, you're also
a very good actress,

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:57.884
and this is so --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.884 --> 00:02:00.186
No, no, but let me say this.
-Can you imagine if I faked it?

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:01.787
-If this was you acting,
I'd be like,

00:02:01.787 --> 00:02:04.490
"Drew, this is so over-the-top."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:06.359
So we're gonna actually play it
so people can hear.

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:07.960
-Oh, my God!

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.796
-Because it is -- We're not
gonna play much.

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:11.831
[ Cheers and applause ]
It's audio only.

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:14.534
-Okay, I do not remember any of
this, except for that I was

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:17.136
like, "I have to tell Seth
and be personal about this."

00:02:17.136 --> 00:02:18.704
What the -- Oh, God.

00:02:18.704 --> 00:02:23.809
-This is like somebody in a very
bad dinner-theater production of

00:02:23.809 --> 00:02:26.112
somebody who's like,
"Play a very sick person."

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:27.380
So let's listen.
-I have heard from every

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:29.882
director I've ever worked
with less.

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:31.784
-[ Gravelly voice ]
Hi, Seth, it's Drew.

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:34.387
I am --
[ Coughing ]

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:35.755
-Oh, my God!

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:40.059
-[ Coughing ]
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:41.995
I can't do your show because

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:44.030
I don't want to do that
on the show.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:46.199
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:49.569
-I realize now you're actually
doing E.T. which is really cool.

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:52.438
[ Laughter ]
-I totally am. I am E.T.

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:54.907
-It's a really good callback
to your early work.

00:02:54.907 --> 00:02:57.277
-God, you never know what
you sound like.

00:02:57.277 --> 00:02:58.944
-But that was very nice
that you did that.

00:02:58.944 --> 00:03:02.314
I mean, especially now, because,
as a fellow talk-show host,

00:03:02.314 --> 00:03:05.017
I think the host would be
the last person who would bail

00:03:05.017 --> 00:03:06.519
at the last minute
unless they absolutely had to.

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:07.987
So I want you to know,
we totally understood.

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:09.588
-I mean, in some ways,
I kind of wish

00:03:09.588 --> 00:03:11.056
I had brought that to the show.

00:03:11.056 --> 00:03:12.358
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:14.426
It would have been
a pretty awesome vibe.

00:03:14.426 --> 00:03:16.862
[ Laughter ]
-That's the thing where it's not

00:03:16.862 --> 00:03:20.533
the right time to make jokes
about wellness.

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:21.701
-Nobody wants that.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.335
Nobody wants that to come out
of the elevator.

00:03:23.335 --> 00:03:26.238
-No, no. But I'm here now!

00:03:26.238 --> 00:03:28.308
-I'm so happy to have you.
And not only are you

00:03:28.308 --> 00:03:29.676
a talk-show host,
but you're a talk-show pro.

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:31.344
You started doing this
at a very young age.

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:33.245
-That's true.
-And we actually have a clip,

00:03:33.245 --> 00:03:37.750
an incredibly precocious clip
of you on "Johnny Carson."

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:40.720
And I mean, you are --
Not only are you a kid,

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.321
but you are just so confident.

00:03:42.321 --> 00:03:43.556
You're more confident than,
I would say,

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:45.792
half the adults I have
on this show.

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:48.894
-And we're both parents, so
we're around younger kids now.

00:03:48.894 --> 00:03:50.863
-Yeah.
-Whereas, when I grew up, I was,

00:03:50.863 --> 00:03:53.466
like, weirded out by kids
'cause I was, like, a working,

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:55.368
you know, paying-the-rent kid.

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:57.503
Didn't go to school,
I didn't have siblings.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:58.871
I was always around adults.

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:00.706
So kids would be like,
"Mah mah mah!"

00:04:00.706 --> 00:04:04.176
and I was like...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.176 --> 00:04:07.647
-You're like, "Do you behave
like that at your job?"

00:04:07.647 --> 00:04:09.415
-Yeah, exactly.
-The kids were like,
"I don't have a job.

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:13.152
I'm seven."
-"Beat it, kid,
you're being a weirdo."

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:17.256
I just was -- I was, um --
I don't know how kids

00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:20.393
are as precocious as they are
or how I was.

00:04:20.393 --> 00:04:23.128
I feel like my life is
so full-circle in that

00:04:23.128 --> 00:04:26.799
I'm much more intimidated
and dialed-back.

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:29.735
When you're a kid,
you don't know to filter.

00:04:29.735 --> 00:04:31.471
-Yes.
-It's like Amy Schumer said

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:33.506
in that cute movie, "I Feel
Pretty," which I love so much.

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:34.907
She's like, "We let our bellies
hang out.

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:37.643
We don't think about it.
We say whatever we want."

00:04:37.643 --> 00:04:42.414
We get older and more
conscientious of what people

00:04:42.414 --> 00:04:45.351
think and feel,
and you start to almost

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:47.286
get shyer as you get older.

00:04:47.286 --> 00:04:48.621
-Well, there was no shyness
here.

00:04:48.621 --> 00:04:51.157
Let's show this clip real quick
of a young Drew.

00:04:51.157 --> 00:04:52.925
-I love New York.

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:56.261
-Why?
-Well, I mean, it's my place.

00:04:56.261 --> 00:05:00.633
I mean, I don't like to go --
I mean, I'm not a person,

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:02.701
really -- I mean, I love L.A.

00:05:02.701 --> 00:05:04.470
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:08.240
-But, um, I like --
I don't like to dress up

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:10.409
in bikinis and go to the beach.

00:05:10.409 --> 00:05:13.446
I like to dress up warm
and be in my thermies

00:05:13.446 --> 00:05:15.581
and go run around the hotel.

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:17.016
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:19.184
Okay, well, none of that
has changed.

00:05:19.184 --> 00:05:20.786
[ Cheers and applause ]
I am the same person.

00:05:20.786 --> 00:05:25.357
-I will say, the crazy thing
to me, is the awareness of

00:05:25.357 --> 00:05:27.893
being in L.A. with an audience,

00:05:27.893 --> 00:05:29.394
as you're doing a talk-show
appearance, and you're like,

00:05:29.394 --> 00:05:32.197
"I love New York. I love L.A.,
too," that even as a kid,

00:05:32.197 --> 00:05:34.000
you were like, "I don't want to
lose the audience here."

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.268
[ Laughter ]

00:05:35.268 --> 00:05:38.170
-Well, the first time I was
on "Carson," I walked up

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:41.273
to the stage and fell
and went, like, splat.

00:05:41.273 --> 00:05:43.809
And that was a good moment
in that

00:05:43.809 --> 00:05:45.778
it never can get worse
than that.

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:47.012
-Yes.
-You know?

00:05:47.012 --> 00:05:51.116
You can't, like, eat it
in your first time out

00:05:51.116 --> 00:05:54.086
on national television and not
go, "Well, you know what?

00:05:54.086 --> 00:05:56.589
Only up from here."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.589 --> 00:05:58.557
No fear and embarrassment
anymore.

00:05:58.557 --> 00:05:59.858
-I have a lot of questions of
what you're doing

00:05:59.858 --> 00:06:01.227
when you're not hosting
your talk show.

00:06:01.227 --> 00:06:02.761
We're gonna be right back
with more

00:06:02.761 --> 00:06:04.530
from Drew Barrymore, everybody.

